+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LkPuyaDfzVhfVPUiea6pXh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Circuit Debugger\n2\t\n3\tBuild a circuit simulator and wire-swap debugger for logic gate circuits.\n4\t\n5\t## Data Model\n6\t\n7\t### Gate\n8\t\n9\t```typescript\n10\tinterface Gate {\n11\t  op: 'AND' | 'OR' | 'XOR';\n12\t  in1: string;   // input wire name\n13\t  in2: string;   // input wire name\n14\t  out: string;   // output wire name\n15\t}\n16\t```\n17\t\n18\tWires are named with arbitrary strings. Some wires follow naming conventions:\n19\t- `x00`, `x01`, ..., `x44` — input bits (X register, bit 0 is least significant)\n20\t- `y00`, `y01`, ..., `y44` — input bits (Y register, bit 0 is least significant)\n21\t- `z00`, `z01`, ..., `z45` — output bits (Z register, bit 0 is least significant)\n22\t- All other wires have random names (e.g., `abc`, `qrs`, `ntg`)\n23\t\n24\t## API\n25\t\n26\tExport two functions from `src/index.ts`:\n27\t\n28\t### `simulate(gates: Gate[], inputs: Record<string, number>): Record<string, number>`\n29\t\n30\tGiven a set of gates and initial wire values (0 or 1), simulate the circuit and return the final value of every wire.\n31\t\n32\tEach gate takes two input wires, applies the operation, and writes to the output wire:\n33\t- **AND**: output is 1 only if both inputs are 1\n34\t- **OR**: output is 1 if at least one input is 1\n35\t- **XOR**: output is 1 if exactly one input is 1\n36\t\n37\tGates can depend on other gates' outputs. Process them in dependency order — a gate can only fire when both its inputs have values. All circuits provided are acyclic (no circular dependencies).\n38\t\n39\t### `findSwappedWires(gates: Gate[]): string[]`\n40\t\n41\tThe gates describe a binary adder circuit that computes `X + Y = Z` where X, Y, and Z are multi-bit binary numbers. The circuit has inputs `x00..xNN` and `y00..yNN`, and outputs `z00..z(N+1)` (one extra bit for carry).\n42\t\n43\tHowever, **exactly 4 pairs of gate output wires have been swapped**. This means 8 gates have incorrect output wire names — each pair had their `out` fields exchanged.\n44\t\n45\tFind all 8 wires involved in swaps and return them as a sorted array of strings.\n46\t\n47\t**Constraint**: Must handle circuits with up to 45 input bits (~220 gates) and return results in under 5 seconds. Brute-force enumeration of swap combinations is not feasible.\n48\t\n49\t## Example: 4-Bit Adder\n50\t\n51\tHere is a correct (un-swapped) 4-bit binary adder. Study its structure — all the circuits you'll debug follow this same pattern but with wires swapped:\n52\t\n53\t```\n54\tx00 XOR y00 -> z00     (bit 0: half adder — just XOR, no prior carry)\n55\tx00 AND y00 -> c00     (bit 0: carry out)\n56\t\n57\tx01 XOR y01 -> t01     (bit 1: partial sum)\n58\tt01 XOR c00 -> z01     (bit 1: final sum = partial XOR carry-in)\n59\tx01 AND y01 -> a01     (bit 1: generate carry)\n60\tt01 AND c00 -> b01     (bit 1: propagate carry)\n61\ta01 OR  b01 -> c01     (bit 1: carry out = generate OR propagate)\n62\t\n63\tx02 XOR y02 -> t02     (bit 2: partial sum)\n64\tt02 XOR c01 -> z02     (bit 2: final sum)\n65\tx02 AND y02 -> a02     (bit 2: generate carry)\n66\tt02 AND c01 -> b02     (bit 2: propagate carry)\n67\ta02 OR  b02 -> c02     (bit 2: carry out)\n68\t\n69\tx03 XOR y03 -> t03     (bit 3: partial sum)\n70\tt03 XOR c02 -> z03     (bit 3: final sum)\n71\tx03 AND y03 -> a03     (bit 3: generate carry)\n72\tt03 AND c02 -> b03     (bit 3: propagate carry)\n73\ta03 OR  b03 -> c03     (bit 3: carry out)\n74\t\n75\tc03 -> z04              (bit 4: final carry becomes MSB of output)\n76\t```\n77\t\n78\tIn a swapped circuit, some gate outputs would be exchanged. For example, if `z01` and `a01` were swapped, the gate that should output `z01` would instead output `a01` and vice versa. The two affected gates would have their `out` fields exchanged. Your job is to find all such swapped output wires.\n79\t\n80\t## Commands\n81\t\n82\t```bash\n83\tnpm test        # run tests\n84\tnpm run build   # compile TypeScript\n85\tnpm run lint    # lint source\n86\t```\n87\t\n88\t## File Structure\n89\t\n90\tPlace your implementation in `src/`. The main entry point should be `src/index.ts`.\n91\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0da26a2-290e-4739-8c99-04a7ee6fb14c","uuid":"20d391e9-25ff-44a0-832c-7b5f33649778","timestamp":"2026-07-01T00:16:47.799Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/TASK.md","content":"# Circuit Debugger\n\nBuild a circuit simulator and wire-swap debugger for logic gate circuits.\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Gate\n\n```typescript\ninterface Gate {\n  op: 'AND' | 'OR' | 'XOR';\n  in1: string;   // input wire name\n  in2: string;   // input wire name\n  out: string;   // output wire name\n}\n```\n\nWires are named with arbitrary strings. Some wires follow naming conventions:\n- `x00`, `x01`, ..., `x44` — input bits (X register, bit 0 is least significant)\n- `y00`, `y01`, ..., `y44` — input bits (Y register, bit 0 is least significant)\n- `z00`, `z01`, ..., `z45` — output bits (Z register, bit 0 is least significant)\n- All other wires have random names (e.g., `abc`, `qrs`, `ntg`)\n\n## API\n\nExport two functions from `src/index.ts`:\n\n### `simulate(gates: Gate[], inputs: Record<string, number>): Record<string, number>`\n\nGiven a set of gates and initial wire values (0 or 1), simulate the circuit and return the final value of every wire.\n\nEach gate takes two input wires, applies the operation, and writes to the output wire:\n- **AND**: output is 1 only if both inputs are 1\n- **OR**: output is 1 if at least one input is 1\n- **XOR**: output is 1 if exactly one input is 1\n\nGates can depend on other gates' outputs. Process them in dependency order — a gate can only fire when both its inputs have values. All circuits provided are acyclic (no circular dependencies).\n\n### `findSwappedWires(gates: Gate[]): string[]`\n\nThe gates describe a binary adder circuit that computes `X + Y = Z` where X, Y, and Z are multi-bit binary numbers. The circuit has inputs `x00..xNN` and `y00..yNN`, and outputs `z00..z(N+1)` (one extra bit for carry).\n\nHowever, **exactly 4 pairs of gate output wires have been swapped**. This means 8 gates have incorrect output wire names — each pair had their `out` fields exchanged.\n\nFind all 8 wires involved in swaps and return them as a sorted array of strings.\n\n**Constraint**: Must handle circuits with up to 45 input bits (~220 gates) and return results in under 5 seconds. Brute-force enumeration of swap combinations is not feasible.\n\n## Example: 4-Bit Adder\n\nHere is a correct (un-swapped) 4-bit binary adder. Study its structure — all the circuits you'll debug follow this same pattern but with wires swapped:\n\n```\nx00 XOR y00 -> z00     (bit 0: half adder — just XOR, no prior carry)\nx00 AND y00 -> c00     (bit 0: carry out)\n\nx01 XOR y01 -> t01     (bit 1: partial sum)\nt01 XOR c00 -> z01     (bit 1: final sum = partial XOR carry-in)\nx01 AND y01 -> a01     (bit 1: generate carry)\nt01 AND c00 -> b01     (bit 1: propagate carry)\na01 OR  b01 -> c01     (bit 1: carry out = generate OR propagate)\n\nx02 XOR y02 -> t02     (bit 2: partial sum)\nt02 XOR c01 -> z02     (bit 2: final sum)\nx02 AND y02 -> a02     (bit 2: generate carry)\nt02 AND c01 -> b02     (bit 2: propagate carry)\na02 OR  b02 -> c02     (bit 2: carry out)\n\nx03 XOR y03 -> t03     (bit 3: partial sum)\nt03 XOR c02 -> z03     (bit 3: final sum)\nx03 AND y03 -> a03     (bit 3: generate carry)\nt03 AND c02 -> b03     (bit 3: propagate carry)\na03 OR  b03 -> c03     (bit 3: carry out)\n\nc03 -> z04              (bit 4: final carry becomes MSB of output)\n```\n\nIn a swapped circuit, some gate outputs would be exchanged. For example, if `z01` and `a01` were swapped, the gate that should output `z01` would instead output `a01` and vice versa. The two affected gates would have their `out` fields exchanged. Your job is to find all such swapped output wires.\n\n## Commands\n\n```bash\nnpm test        # run tests\nnpm run build   # compile TypeScript\nnpm run lint    # lint source\n```\n\n## File Structure\n\nPlace your implementation in `src/`. The main entry point should be `src/index.ts`.\n","numLines":91,"startLine":1,"totalLines":91}}}
